'''Behemoth Culling''' is a group of stages and [[Catnip Challenges|missions]] centered around [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth Enemies]].

==Stages==
Similar to [[Empress' Research]], Behemoth Culling maps appear for 4 set hours of every day and disappear until the next day when cleared. The main three maps initially have four stages each. Upon clearing the fourth stage in each map, a new, single-stage map titled Affliction in the Forest, Oddity in the Desert, or Peril in the Volcano will start to appear with the same schedule, which will unlock six extra stages for the corresponding map when cleared. Another Afflication/Oddity/Peril event will appear after clearing the 10th and 16th stages of each map, again unlocking further stages when completed. The 20th and final stages drop 1 [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Cat Ticket]] upon first completion and need to be beaten in map order: beating [[Hidden Forest of Gapra]]'s [[Stormrent Forest Area: Final]] unlocks [[Ashvini Desert]]'s [[Moon Dust Area: Final]], which in turn unlocks [[Jinfore Volcano]]'s [[Ancient Volcano Area: Final]].

Clearing the Behemoth Culling stages is one of the few ways to obtain [[Catfruit|Behemoth Stones]] to evolve certain cats. Each map offers a different selection of Behemoth Stones and [[Ototo Corps|materials]] for the [[Cat Base]]; the further you progress, the higher the Behemoth Stone drop rates and the lower the chance for materials. Note that Epic Behemoth Stones are not obtainable from these stages and currently only drop from [[Mining Epic]], an unrelated event unlocked after clearing [[Atonement for Sin]].

